# Template for /root/pve-config/secrets.env.
#
# The real file lives on the host at mode 600 and is never committed. It is
# kept separate from pve-config.conf so that the configuration the toolkit
# rewrites on every run can never pick up a credential, and so the values
# here stay out of the logs.
#
#   cp examples/secrets.env.example /root/pve-config/secrets.env
#   chmod 600 /root/pve-config/secrets.env
#
# Each value may also be supplied as an environment variable. That does not
# make it a one-off. The driver resolves the whole schema before any stage
# runs and writes the resolved secrets back here at mode 600, so an
# exported value lands in this file -- including over a blank placeholder
# like the ones below. A stage that needs a credential at run time also
# persists its own copy. See the key notes below for where each one lands,
# and treat the environment as a way to get a value in, not a way to keep
# it off disk.

# DNS Made Easy API credentials for the ACME DNS-01 challenge.
# Issued at https://cp.dnsmadeeasy.com/account/info
# The certificate stage copies these into /etc/pve-config/dnsmadeeasy.conf
# at mode 600 and hands pvenode the path, so neither value reaches a
# command line. pvenode then keeps a base64 copy of its own under
# /etc/pve/priv/acme/plugins.cfg. Rotate at DNS Made Easy to retire them;
# removing them from here removes neither copy.
# Either name set in the environment wins over the value here, which is how
# a rotation reaches the host first -- and the driver then writes the new
# value into this file. An empty one in the environment stops the stage
# rather than falling back to this file.
PVE_DNSMADEEASY_KEY=''
PVE_DNSMADEEASY_SECRET=''

# Tailscale pre-authentication key for the Tailscale LXC. Generate a
# reusable, ephemeral-free key in the admin console and disable key expiry
# on the node afterwards, or the tunnel drops months later.
PVE_TAILSCALE_AUTHKEY=''

# Zulip bot credentials for boot and shutdown notices. Only needed when
# PVE_ZULIP_ENABLED is yes.
PVE_ZULIP_SITE='https://example.zulipchat.com'
PVE_ZULIP_BOT_EMAIL='pve-bot@example.zulipchat.com'
PVE_ZULIP_BOT_API_KEY=''
